<article class="env-lemma" id="0GD2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GD2">Lemma <span data-tag="0GD2">88.20.6</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ and $g : Y \to Z$ be morphisms of locally Noetherian formal algebraic spaces over $S$. If $f$ and $g$ are rig-étale, then so is $g \circ f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Formal Spaces, Remark <a href="/tag/0GBK" data-tag="0GBK">87.21.14</a> this follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/0GCX" data-tag="0GCX">88.19.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>